  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Global Communications recorded $504M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS received 114 awards with an average award size of $4.4M. L3HARRIS obligations are down 37.2% year over year. L3HARRIS has a strong concentration in a single buyer. The Department of Defense obligated $504M to L3HARRIS. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $478K and the Department of the Interior obligated $0. L3HARRIS wins are concentrated in a few NAICS markets. Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $492M, Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $10.3M, and Fluid Power Cylinder and Actuator Manufacturing accounts for $1.3M. L3HARRIS also shows smaller obligations in Satellite Telecommunications ($75K), Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing ($440K), and several other minor markets. Historical obligations show a peak in FY24 at $1B and a recent decline from FY25 obligations of $803M to the current FY26 total of $504M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who is buying from L3HARRIS Global Communications?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $504M to L3HARRIS in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $478K. The Department of the Interior shows $0 in obligations for the current period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive L3HARRIS Global Communications revenue?",
        "body": "Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing is the largest market for L3HARRIS, accounting for $492M in FY2026 to date. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $10.3M and Fluid Power Cylinder and Actuator Manufacturing accounts for $1.3M. Smaller markets include Satellite Telecommunications ($75K) and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing ($440K)."
      }
    ]
